// fs-v2-r5 (a): short atomic copies of a buffered write by the process "notear": ext4's
// write_end (ext4_da_write_end, delalloc: C's default) called with copied < len, keyed by
// where the copied prefix ends in the file page ((pos + copied) % 4096) and copied: a cut at 0
// is a page cut, anything else a mid-page cut, which write_end commits when the folio is
// uptodate (the file's page cached, as here: the file was written and synced first). copied = 0
// is a copy that stopped at once (generic_perform_write then faults the source in).
// (copy_folio_from_iter_atomic and fault_in_iov_iter_readable are not traceable on this kernel.)
kprobe:ext4_da_write_end /comm == "notear"/ {
  @calls = count();
  if (arg4 < arg3) { @short[(arg2 + arg4) % 4096, arg4] = count(); }
}
